{
  "$schema": "../gen/schemas/desktop-schema.json",
  "identifier": "main",
  "description": "What the main application window may invoke. SEC-IPC-001 and SEC-IPC-003: since build.rs declares an application ACL manifest, a custom command is reachable only from a window whose capability names it, so this list is the enforced surface rather than a description of one. The window label is the security identity; it is named exactly and never as a wildcard, so a second window does not inherit this set by existing. Every entry here is also classified in security/command-policy.json, and the companion tests fail if the two disagree or if a registered command appears in neither. Entries are ordered by risk class, weakest first: local session, diagnostics, reads, writes, membership and roles, durable authority, OS handoff, local media. Core window permissions cover our own title bar because decorations are off; destroy runs only after the close handler finishes the native vault lock and snapshot. The updater and process pair lets the app check for a signed release and relaunch into it once the user accepts.",
